[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axes derived from the C source, not guessed:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Runtime options / modes.** The library has exactly one: `driver`'s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `int useGood` parameter, which drives `if (useGood) good(); else bad();`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`driver.c:74-83`). Two states: zero → `bad`, non-zero → `good`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   There are no other flags, no globals, no `#ifdef`, no `switch`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **`#ifdef` / compile-time branches.** `grep -c '#if' src/driver.c` → only the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `DRIVER_H_` include guard in the header. No conditional code.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Public entry points (full set, lowest level first).** From `nm -D`, not from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `driver.h` — the header only declares `driver`, but four more functions are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   exported and callable by any consumer:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   1. `printIntLine(int)` — lowest level, formats one `int`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   2. `printLine(const char*)` — lowest level, guarded by a null check.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   3. `bad()` — composes `printIntLine` over an under-allocated `alloca`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   4. `good()` — composes `printIntLine` over a correctly sized `alloca`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   5. `driver(int)` — the convenience/one-shot wrapper over `bad`/`good`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Rows below exercise 1–4 **directly**, not only through 5.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Input shapes the code distinguishes.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * `printIntLine`: sign and magnitude of the `int` (`%d` formatting) —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     negative / zero / positive, and the `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` extremes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * `printLine`: null vs non-null (the only branch), then length
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     (empty / 1 byte / many / very long) and byte content (ASCII / format
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     metacharacters / embedded newlines / high non-UTF-8 bytes).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * `bad`/`good`: no parameters; the shape axis is the *allocation size*
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     (10 bytes vs 40 bytes) and the fixed count 10 of the copy loop. Their only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     observable is `data[0]`, always `source[0] == 0`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   * Sequencing/state shape: repeated and interleaved calls, since `bad()`'s
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     stack overrun could otherwise perturb later calls differently in the two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     implementations.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
